[{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[exp] tries to simplify each PropagatorDenominator in a canonical way. FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[exp, q1] simplifies all FeynAmpDenominators in exp in a canonical way, including momentum shifts. Scaleless integrals are discarded.","anchor":"feynampdenominatorsimplify"},{"text":"Overview, TID.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FDS","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\text{FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify}","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The cornerstone of dimensional regularization is that \\int d^n k f(k)/k^4 = 0","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[f[k] FAD[k, k], k]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"This brings some loop integrals into a standard form.","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[FAD[k - Subscript[p, 1], k - Subscript[p, 2]], k]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{k^2.(k-p_1+p_2){}^2}\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[FAD[k, k, k - q], k]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\frac{1}{\\left(k^2\\right)^2.(k-q)^2}","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[f[k] FAD[k, k - q, k - q], k]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\frac{f(q-k)}{\\left(k^2\\right)^2.(k-q)^2}","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify[FAD[k - Subscript[p, 1], k - Subscript[p, 2]] SPD[k, k], k] ApartFF[%, {k}] TID[%, k] // Factor2","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{2 \\left(k\\cdot p_2\\right)+k^2+p_2{}^2}{k^2.(k-p_1+p_2){}^2}\\]","anchor":"cb6-5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{2 \\left(k\\cdot p_2\\right)+p_2{}^2}{k^2.(k-p_1+p_2){}^2}\\]","anchor":"cb6-5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p_1\\cdot p_2}{k^2.(k-p_1+p_2){}^2}\\]","anchor":"cb6-5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FDS[FAD[k - p1, k - p2] SPD[k, OPEDelta]^2, k]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{(k\\cdot \\Delta +\\Delta \\cdot \\;\\text{p2})^2}{k^2.(k-\\text{p1}+\\text{p2})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"}]